<PolicyPage title="Corrections - Love Mallacoota" description="How to request and how we record corrections on Love Mallacoota." canonicalPath="/corrections.html" prefix="Fast, visible" accent="Corrections" lede="If something is wrong, we fix it promptly and keep an accountable record of significant changes.">
  <h2>Request a correction</h2>
  <p>Use the <a href="/contact.html">update form</a> and include the page, the current information, the correction and the best available source. A group or business may also ask for its own listing to be removed.</p>
  <h2>How we respond</h2>
  <p>We verify the request in proportion to its impact. Straightforward directory corrections are made as soon as practical. Disputed or safety-related claims may require confirmation from an authoritative source.</p>
  <h2>Correction record</h2>
  <p>Minor spelling and formatting fixes may be made silently. Material corrections should carry a dated note or be traceable through the public repository history, including why the change was made.</p>
  <h2>Right of reply</h2>
  <p>If published information about a local organisation or business is materially wrong, it can request a correction or removal without having to argue its case publicly.</p>
</PolicyPage>
